15:08.173 --> 15:12.473
I am going to the top, and there's nothing
you or anyone else can do about it.

15:13.178 --> 15:15.510
Who the hell does he think he is?

15:29.595 --> 15:31.153
Come on. Come on.

15:31.530 --> 15:32.588
Go away!

15:36.035 --> 15:37.468
We now return to...

15:37.569 --> 15:38.536
Mmm-mmmh.

15:39.438 --> 15:40.996
Mmm-hmmm.

15:41.273 --> 15:42.433
Mmm-hmmmh.

15:42.675 --> 15:43.642
Mmm-hmmm.

15:47.446 --> 15:48.777
Hey, there, sweetie.

15:48.881 --> 15:50.974
I got a wax this morning,
and let's just say...

15:51.083 --> 15:53.210
- you're cleared for landing, huh?
- Giggidy!

15:53.319 --> 15:54.809
Lois, what the hell's up with you lately?

15:54.920 --> 15:57.184
You're acting all weird,
and you're staying out all night.

15:57.289 --> 16:00.850
I was just out with some of the girls,
and you're not gonna believe this.

16:00.960 --> 16:04.020
I got invited to a Vogue magazine party.

16:05.331 --> 16:08.425
That guest list is more exclusive
than the Garden of Eden.

16:08.534 --> 16:11.901
So, basically, you can eat from
any tree you want, except this one.

16:12.004 --> 16:12.971
Can we sit underneath it?

16:13.305 --> 16:15.830
You know,
I would just not go near it at all.

16:18.811 --> 16:22.508
Brian, thanks for showing up so promptly
for your quarterly evaluation.

16:22.614 --> 16:25.811
Now, then. I'm going to do something
I call the compliment sandwich...

16:25.918 --> 16:28.944
where I say something good, then talk
about where you need improvement...

16:29.054 --> 16:30.487
and then end with something good.

16:30.589 --> 16:31.749
Whatever you gotta do.

16:31.857 --> 16:33.188
Okay.

16:33.292 --> 16:36.056
Let's see. Something good.
Something good. Something good.

16:36.862 --> 16:39.729
You look like Snoopy,
and it makes me smile.

16:40.599 --> 16:42.362
Where you need improvement.

16:42.768 --> 16:44.827
You have smelly dog farts.

16:45.504 --> 16:47.062
Something good. Something good.

16:47.306 --> 16:50.833
You really dazzled that rep
from the Cincinnati office last week.

16:51.443 --> 16:55.436
That is sensationaI. You really made me
feeI confident about those numbers.

16:55.547 --> 16:57.708
Listen, if you're ever looking
for a change of scenery...

16:57.816 --> 17:00.444
we could sure use
a fellow like you in Cincinnati.

17:00.552 --> 17:02.213
- That was you in disguise.
- No, it wasn't.

17:02.321 --> 17:03.288
- Yes, it was.
- No, it wasn't.

17:03.389 --> 17:05.084
- Fine, it wasn't.
- It was.

17:07.960 --> 17:09.552
Mr. Pewterschmidt, I need your help.

17:09.661 --> 17:11.094
Lois is out of controI.

17:11.196 --> 17:14.723
I mean, she's acting crazier than I did
that time I tried Ecstasy.

17:16.668 --> 17:21.332
Oh, Brian, your fur is so soft.

17:22.541 --> 17:24.372
Oh, your ears.

17:24.877 --> 17:27.505
Your ears are like dog ears.

17:28.047 --> 17:31.107
Oh, this couch.

17:33.986 --> 17:37.888
Stewie, your head is so smooth.

17:38.490 --> 17:41.425
How is that even... How you doing that?

17:41.827 --> 17:43.158
How you doing that?

17:43.429 --> 17:46.830
Oh! Everything here is fantastic.

17:50.169 --> 17:53.002
Oh, these clothes.

18:06.151 --> 18:08.016
I'm really worried about her,
Mr. Pewterschmidt...

18:08.120 --> 18:11.214
and I figured I'd come to you since
you were always good at reeling her in.

18:11.323 --> 18:13.757
Well, Lois was always a wild stallion...

18:13.859 --> 18:15.759
but don't worry.
I know how to controI her.

18:15.861 --> 18:16.987
And I'll help you...

18:17.096 --> 18:19.428
but first, you have to do something for me.

18:19.531 --> 18:20.793
Eat this pine cone.

18:20.899 --> 18:23.231
- Well...
- Eat it. It will amuse me.

18:25.137 --> 18:27.662
- How is it? How does it taste?
- It's awfuI.

18:27.806 --> 18:29.706
- Finish it. Eat it.
- I hate it.

18:29.808 --> 18:31.639
Eat it. Eat it. Swallow it.

18:31.743 --> 18:34.303
- It hurts.
- This is for Lois. Go on.

18:34.413 --> 18:38.042
- It hurts!
- Good.

18:38.150 --> 18:39.378
- all right. We good to go?
- Yup.

18:44.456 --> 18:46.219
all right, how's my man-tan?

18:46.325 --> 18:47.553
There we go. all set.

18:47.659 --> 18:49.786
Good. A little body glitter for you.

18:50.062 --> 18:53.463
Yeah. Yeah. That's hot. That's hot.
all right, let's do this.

18:54.433 --> 18:56.833
- What are you doing? Like... obvious.
- Shut up.

18:56.935 --> 18:58.459
Check out these ribs, Lois.

18:58.570 --> 19:00.561
Oh, yeah? That's nothing.

19:01.273 --> 19:02.865
Go ahead. Try them out.

19:08.013 --> 19:09.503
Hey, not bad.

19:17.256 --> 19:18.621
- You see Jimmy Smits in there?
- Yeah.

19:18.724 --> 19:19.816
Yeah, that was cooI.

19:21.793 --> 19:23.556
So, what did you wanna see me about?

19:23.662 --> 19:26.631
You know, Brian, there was a note
in the suggestion box that says:

19:26.732 --> 19:29.166
"Stewie should eat a steaming bag of... "

19:29.601 --> 19:32.627
Well, I'm not gonna say the last word,
but I think you know what it is.

19:32.738 --> 19:36.504
Look, Brian, a corporation
is a lot like a centipede.

19:36.942 --> 19:40.378
It only works if all the legs are moving
toward the same end.

19:41.013 --> 19:42.913
And you know what you are, Brian?

19:43.015 --> 19:44.915
- You're a busted leg.
- What?

19:45.450 --> 19:46.417
Are you firing me?

19:46.518 --> 19:48.782
Don't think about coming back
and shooting up the place...

19:48.887 --> 19:50.184
because security has your picture.

19:52.524 --> 19:54.321
What the hell are you guys doing?

19:54.426 --> 19:57.554
You're not leaving this room untiI
you agree to stop this modeling thing...

19:57.663 --> 19:58.652
once and for all.

19:58.764 --> 20:00.561
This isn't gonna work, you guys.

20:00.666 --> 20:03.567
Why can't you understand
I'm doing what I want?

20:03.669 --> 20:05.534
Jeez, Carter, what are we doing?

20:05.637 --> 20:07.901
I mean, if Lois wants to be a modeI...

20:08.106 --> 20:09.767
we don't got any right to stop her.

20:09.875 --> 20:12.036
You really mean that, Peter?

20:12.144 --> 20:14.612
Of course, I do.
I just want you to be happy.

20:14.713 --> 20:17.181
This is ridiculous.
No daughter of mine is going to be happy.

20:17.282 --> 20:19.750
Excuse me, Carter. I think I owe you this.

20:20.419 --> 20:22.819
That's for giving me a book last Christmas.

20:22.921 --> 20:24.388
You're rich, you jerk.

20:24.489 --> 20:28.220
Well, Lois, I guess you should go ahead
and get back to your party.

20:29.161 --> 20:30.150
What's wrong?

20:30.262 --> 20:33.254
Aren't you gonna go do your little turn
on the catwalk, Lois?

20:33.365 --> 20:34.525
On the catwalk?

20:34.633 --> 20:36.123
Yeah, on the catwalk?

20:36.335 --> 20:37.996
Do your little turn on the catwalk?

20:38.103 --> 20:40.037
Well, now that you say
you're fine with it...

20:40.138 --> 20:43.369
to be honest, I'm not really sure
I wanna do it anymore.

20:43.809 --> 20:47.040
I think all I really wanted
was the freedom to know I could...

20:47.346 --> 20:49.576
and now I have it because I have you.

20:49.681 --> 20:51.342
You sure do, Lois.

20:52.818 --> 20:54.718
What are we gonna do with him?

20:55.087 --> 20:56.748
Hey, you wanna make him
really mad, Lois?

20:56.855 --> 20:59.346
Let's have sex on his back like we used to.

21:01.460 --> 21:03.189
What the hell's going on?

21:03.190 --> 22:04.190
Thank you for watching «Family Guy» on
www.FOX-fan.ru